From 3692b635678ec1c66f63f320cce39f88126933b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Polonsky <ifnotelse@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 17:48:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] DAOS-XXXXX dfs: Return scan statistics and scan
 subdirectories

daos fs scan walks a POSIX container and reports how many files,
directories and symlinks it has and how many bytes its files hold. The
statistics are only printed to stdout by libdfs, so neither applications
nor the daos tool can use them, and --dir-name is accepted but ignored:
the scan always starts from the root (a TODO in dfs_cont_scan()).

Add dfs_scan(), which walks the tree under an open directory of a mounted
DFS and returns the statistics in a dfs_scan_stats_t. Progress is printed
only with DFS_SCAN_PRINT_PROGRESS. dfs_cont_scan() keeps its signature and
output, now uses dfs_scan() and honors the subdirectory, with or without
a leading /.

daos fs scan now calls dfs_scan() through fs_scan_hdlr(), so --dir-name
works, and supports -j. It opens the container read-only as the other
fs commands do, and its text output is unchanged.

Add a DFS unit test and document the command.

Features: dfs

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
