   should be visible to another client with a simple coordination between the
   clients.
 
+### Namespace Statistics
+
+`daos fs scan` walks the namespace of a POSIX container and reports the number
+of files, directories and symbolic links, the depth of the tree, the largest
+file and directory, and the total size of the files. `--dir-name` limits the
+scan to a subdirectory, and `-j` prints the result as JSON:
+
+```bash
+$ daos fs scan tank mycont --dir-name /projects/a -j
+```
+
+The total is the sum of the logical file sizes (`st_size`). It does not include
+redundancy (replication or erasure coding), metadata, snapshots, or data not yet
+reclaimed by aggregation, and holes in sparse files are counted. The walk takes
+time proportional to the number of entries and is not atomic. Applications can
+get the same statistics from `dfs_scan()`.
+
 ## Unified NameSpace (UNS)
 
 Many clients support links to other containers as a layer on top of DFS, where a directory in a
